Description:
 linuxmuster-tools7 - Tools for the linuxmuster.net 7 server.
Changes:
 linuxmuster-tools7 (7.4.19) lmn74; urgency=medium
 .
   * [security] [quotas] get_user_quotas() passes the administrator
     password to smbcquotas through the PASSWD environment variable
     instead of its argv, where any local user could read it in the
     process list.
   * [security] [linbo] The .macct files of an uploaded image, which hold
     the Samba secrets of a client, are set to 0600 in the image
     directory and in its backups, and the .incoming staging directory
     to 0700: the [linbo] rsync module serves the LINBO directory
     without login. See #44, reported by @TomlDev.
   * [devices] New validator for devices.csv. Devices.check_conf()
     reports every problem instead of a flat list of sentences, and
     returns a dict (valid, counts, findings, report) instead of a list
     of strings or False: callers have to adapt. Each finding carries a
     stable code to branch on (e.g. hostname.too_long), the offending
     value, and the file and line to fix. The report holds one short
     line per problem, e.g. "❌ ip.invalid 999.999.999.999
     (devices.csv:12)". The 15 characters limit of a hostname only
     applies to the roles getting a machine account. The new
     check_all_schools() validates every school at once, the only way to
     see a host name or a mac address used in two schools; an ip address
     shared between two schools is a warning only (ip.multischool), a
     fileserver legitimately carries the same one in each. The
     module-level COMPUTER_ROLES variable is removed.
   * [devices] Each device exposes macRaw, the address as written in the
     file (mac is None for a malformed one), and csvLine, its physical
     line in devices.csv.
   * [lmnconfig] sophomorix.ini is read with its tabs expanded:
     configparser read a key indented deeper than the previous one as a
     continuation of its value, and 53 keys of the shipped file were
     lost that way, among them the COMPUTER_ACCOUNT of all 15 computer
     roles.
   * [lmnconfig] New SophomorixIni.computer_roles: the computer roles
     split on their COMPUTER_ACCOUNT flag (accounts, dns_only), the
     default role and the full list (roles). SophomorixIni.computerrole
     is deprecated in favour of computer_roles.roles.
   * [lmnconfig] custom_fields.yml is cached per school and read again
     only when its mtime changes. The ldapconnector parsed it on every
     request: listing all users with /users went from 13 s to under a
     second.
   * [common] New natural sorting helpers, natural_key() and
     sort_naturally(): m5 comes before m10, and r100-pc5 before
     r100-pc10. With digitless_last=True, names without any digit come
     last (5a, 10b, abitur). Applied to the sortkey of the ldap_reader,
     the schoolclasses, projects and printers of a user, the lists of
     Devices, the LINBO images and list_workstations().
   * [common] A LINBO group name may only hold letters, digits, _ and -,
     as sophomorix-device accepts it: . and + are refused.
   * [linbo] initcache is accepted with or without a download type;
     without one, linbo-remote takes the one of the start.conf. It
     could never pass the command check before. Fix #42, reported by
     @TomlDev.
   * [linbo] LINBO change tracker: a file changed in the same second as
     the cursor or during the scan was never reported; it now can be
     reported twice, never lost. A file whose mtime can not be read
     counts as changed. The deletedHosts and deletedStartConfs fields,
     always empty, are removed: a deleted entry is the one missing from
     allHostMacs or allStartConfIds. Fix #38, reported by @TomlDev.
   * [linbo] New list_onboot_commands(), get_onboot_command() and
     delete_onboot_command(), to read and withdraw the commands
     linbo-remote -p leaves for a host's next boot.
   * [linbo] New restart_image_services(), restarting linbo-multicast and
     linbo-torrent after a change on an image, and raising on failure
     instead of failing silently.
   * [lmnfile] LMNFile accepts a pathlib.Path as well as a str, and its
     __init__ runs once instead of twice per instantiation.
   * [lmnfile] CSV files expose line_numbers, the physical line of each
     row returned by read().
   * [ldapconnector] Creating the Student-Parents OU failed when the
     Parents OU of the school had no child OU yet; its DN is now built
     from the school instead of the DN of the student.
   * [packaging] postinst no longer runs create_students_groups.py on
     every upgrade: the subgroups of the schoolclasses are kept in sync
     by sophomorix, and the sweep was slow and failed the whole package
     configuration whenever LDAP was down. The script is deprecated, use
     "lmncli schoolclass sync" to repair a class.
